        {
          "id": "qss_step200_row20_col21_ice_and_snow_budget_rescaling",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_quarter_ss idealized supercell (GNU real32 build, dx = 2 km, dt = 12 s, 40 layers, WSM6 only), step 200 (t = 40 min), row j = 20, column i = 21 dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump with the esm_dump_inner hooks inside mp_wsm6_run of the ctessum-claude/MMM-physics fork, commit 52cfbd7) and replayed through the real64 (kind_phys = real64) standalone kernels/wsm6_driver at the WRF step (dtcld = 12 s). POINTWISE in the sense of FORTRAN_BUGS.md N3: the mass-conservation rescaling and the update it feeds are dtcld-dependent by construction (every factor is 1 in the dtcld -> 0 limit), so the test compares them at the kernel's own sub-step instead of replaying at a small dt. Inputs are the state at which the kernel evaluates its rates (t_rates, q/qc/qi/qr/qs/qg_rates, i.e. after the sub-step's sedimentation, melting and freezing), the start-of-sub-step xl and cpm (note N4) and the 22 dumped `<rate>_raw` rates (each after its own per-process limiter, before this block); the expected values are the dumped `<rate>_final` rates, the dumped `*_upd` state and the tendencies (q_upd - q_rates)/dtcld and (t_upd - t_rates)/dtcld from the same replay. The conservation factors are read back from the dump as the ratio of a rate that carries exactly ONE factor (prevp -> f_qr, pidep -> f_qi, psdep -> f_qs, pgdep -> f_qg). This block contains no physical constant beyond T0, xls, qmin, qcrmin and the 1e-4 kg/kg partition threshold, and every input is dumped, so the real64 replay is reproduced to machine precision. Regime: the growing updraft of the early storm -- cloud water 2.6e-4, rain 3.5e-4, cloud ice 5.5e-6, snow 4.6e-6 and graupel 2.2e-5 kg/kg, 7 layers above 0 C. This is the column in which the CLOUD-ICE and SNOW budgets bind: deposition, aggregation and the three ice-collection terms would overdraw the young ice, so f_qi = 0.9738/0.9695/0.9708 at layers 8/9/10, and at layer 8 the snow being produced is itself overdrawn, f_qs = 0.9736 -- so psaut and psaci there carry the PRODUCT f_qi f_qs, which is exactly the sequential cascade this component reproduces with cumulative factors. The rain and graupel budgets are not overdrawn (f_qr = f_qg = 1). Residual (esm vs the real64 replay, measured with zero tolerances): all 22 `<rate>_final` columns, the switches and all seven updated fields are reproduced EXACTLY (0.0); nonzero only in dqv_dt 7.2e-20 kg/kg/s (1.4e-13 of the column maximum), dT_dt 2.1e-15 K/s (1.6e-12 of the column maximum) and one ulp (1.1e-16 relative) in the f_qi spot check at layer 8, where the factor is a quotient of two sums. Tolerances are set at 1e-9 of each rate column's maximum, 1e-12 of each updated field's maximum and rel 1e-12 on the factor spot checks; the switches keep zero tolerance.",
