        {
          "id": "qss_step250_row23_col24_mature_storm_update",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_quarter_ss idealized supercell (GNU real32 build, dx = 2 km, dt = 12 s, 40 layers, WSM6 only), step 250 (t = 50 min), row j = 23, column i = 24 dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump with the esm_dump_inner hooks inside mp_wsm6_run of the ctessum-claude/MMM-physics fork, commit 52cfbd7) and replayed through the real64 (kind_phys = real64) standalone kernels/wsm6_driver at the WRF step (dtcld = 12 s). POINTWISE in the sense of FORTRAN_BUGS.md N3: the mass-conservation rescaling and the update it feeds are dtcld-dependent by construction (every factor is 1 in the dtcld -> 0 limit), so the test compares them at the kernel's own sub-step instead of replaying at a small dt. Inputs are the state at which the kernel evaluates its rates (t_rates, q/qc/qi/qr/qs/qg_rates, i.e. after the sub-step's sedimentation, melting and freezing), the start-of-sub-step xl and cpm (note N4) and the 22 dumped `<rate>_raw` rates (each after its own per-process limiter, before this block); the expected values are the dumped `<rate>_final` rates, the dumped `*_upd` state and the tendencies (q_upd - q_rates)/dtcld and (t_upd - t_rates)/dtcld from the same replay. The conservation factors are read back from the dump as the ratio of a rate that carries exactly ONE factor (prevp -> f_qr, pidep -> f_qi, psdep -> f_qs, pgdep -> f_qg). This block contains no physical constant beyond T0, xls, qmin, qcrmin and the 1e-4 kg/kg partition threshold, and every input is dumped, so the real64 replay is reproduced to machine precision. Regime: the mature storm core, the same column as the warm_rain, cold_accretion and ice_deposition tests -- cloud water 2.3e-3, rain 1.2e-2, cloud ice 3.9e-4, snow 2.1e-3 and graupel 1.1e-2 kg/kg, freezing level at layer 9, 8 layers above 0 C. NO budget is overdrawn here (every factor is 1 to within 1e-16), so this regime tests the other half of the block: the update itself in both branches -- the ice branch with all five species and the delta2/delta3 partition of piacr, praci, psacr and pracs between snow and graupel, and, in the 8 lowest layers, the warm branch in which cloud ice is untouched, the accreted cloud water becomes rain (paacw enters qr twice) and the latent heating is vaporization plus the fusion of the melting terms only. Residual (esm vs the real64 replay, measured with zero tolerances): all 22 `<rate>_final` columns, the switches and six of the seven updated fields are reproduced EXACTLY (0.0); nonzero only in qc_upd 1.1e-19 kg/kg (5.7e-17 of the column maximum), dqv_dt 7.0e-20 kg/kg/s (4.1e-15 of the column maximum) and dT_dt 2.3e-15 K/s (1.9e-14 of the column maximum). Tolerances are set at 1e-9 of each rate column's maximum, 1e-12 of each updated field's maximum and rel 1e-12 on the factor spot checks; the switches keep zero tolerance.",
