        {
          "id": "scm_call120_cirrus_ice_layers_20_to_59",
          "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column case (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, full physics suite: RRTM, Dudhia, sfclayrev, slab, YSU, WSM6), microphysics call 120 (t = 2 h) dumped by the instrumented ctessum-claude/WRF fork (module_esm_dump with the esm_dump_inner hooks inside mp_wsm6_run of the ctessum-claude/MMM-physics fork, commit 52cfbd7) and replayed through the real64 (kind_phys = real64) standalone kernels/wsm6_driver at the WRF step (dtcld = 60 s). POINTWISE in the sense of FORTRAN_BUGS.md N3: the mass-conservation rescaling and the update it feeds are dtcld-dependent by construction (every factor is 1 in the dtcld -> 0 limit), so the test compares them at the kernel's own sub-step instead of replaying at a small dt. Inputs are the state at which the kernel evaluates its rates (t_rates, q/qc/qi/qr/qs/qg_rates, i.e. after the sub-step's sedimentation, melting and freezing), the start-of-sub-step xl and cpm (note N4) and the 22 dumped `<rate>_raw` rates (each after its own per-process limiter, before this block); the expected values are the dumped `<rate>_final` rates, the dumped `*_upd` state and the tendencies (q_upd - q_rates)/dtcld and (t_upd - t_rates)/dtcld from the same replay. The conservation factors are read back from the dump as the ratio of a rate that carries exactly ONE factor (prevp -> f_qr, pidep -> f_qi, psdep -> f_qs, pgdep -> f_qg). This block contains no physical constant beyond T0, xls, qmin, qcrmin and the 1e-4 kg/kg partition threshold, and every input is dumped, so the real64 replay is reproduced to machine precision. Regime: the SCM's thin cirrus layer, levels 20 to 59 of the 59-layer column (an esm-spec 6.6 test cannot rebind the metaparameter NLEV, format gap (j), so the window is taken as the component's 40 levels). Cloud ice reaches 4.5e-5 kg/kg near level 53 and is the only condensate: pidep and pigen are the only nonzero rates, no budget is overdrawn (all eight factors are exactly 1) and the warm branch covers the lower part of the window. The regime pins the identity path -- the rescaling must not perturb rates it does not limit -- and the pure deposition/nucleation update of a cold cirrus layer, four orders of magnitude below the supercell rates. Residual (esm vs the real64 replay, measured with zero tolerances): all 22 `<rate>_final` columns, the switches and all seven updated fields are reproduced EXACTLY (0.0); nonzero only in dqv_dt 2.1e-19 kg/kg/s (6.2e-12 of the column maximum) and dT_dt 1.7e-16 K/s (1.8e-12 of the column maximum). Tolerances are set at 1e-9 of each rate column's maximum, 1e-12 of each updated field's maximum and rel 1e-12 on the factor spot checks; the switches keep zero tolerance.",
